IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg1-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (dg1-seat.l4): at least one case per question, in the facts a person in the seat would
-- state. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of sections 101 to 116 (the line numbers are in the
-- layer-1 modules' quotations), beside the assertion, and was decided before the module was run. T and F in the comments
-- are TRUE and FALSE. Where the text does not decide, the case asserts NOTHING.

§ `Cases for the seat layer`

§§ `Forming the corporation (sections 101 to 107)`

-- Priya, a founder, asks whether she may incorporate, as an individual; then for an LLC; then for a stock corporation.
#ASSERT `May I incorporate a Delaware corporation` `a natural person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I incorporate a Delaware corporation` (`a corporation` `a stock corporation`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I incorporate a Delaware corporation` `a limited liability company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Her business is lawful and no law bars it; then one that another law prohibits.
#ASSERT `May the corporation be formed for this business or these purposes` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation be formed for this business or these purposes` TRUE TRUE)
-- A water utility operating in Delaware is also subject to Title 26; one operating wholly elsewhere is not.
#ASSERT `Is my public utility corporation also subject to Title 26` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my public utility corporation also subject to Title 26` TRUE FALSE)
-- A certificate of merger filed under a section that amends the certificate counts as part of it; the original does; a filing that does not amend does not.
#ASSERT `Does this instrument count as part of my corporation's certificate of incorporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this instrument count as part of my corporation's certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this instrument count as part of my corporation's certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A certified copy proves due execution and filing; an uncertified copy proves nothing under the section.
#ASSERT `Will a certified copy be received as prima facie evidence of this matter` TRUE TRUE `due execution, acknowledgment and filing of the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will a certified copy be received as prima facie evidence of this matter` FALSE TRUE `due execution, acknowledgment and filing of the instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Will a certified copy be received as prima facie evidence of this matter` TRUE TRUE `a matter that is not a fact of those kinds` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The certificate was filed on 10 March 2026: the corporation exists from that date; with a stated later date of 1 April 2026, from then; a later date beyond the ninetieth day is not covered.
#ASSERT `From what date does my corporation exist` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `From what date does my corporation exist` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `From what date does my corporation exist` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `From what date does my corporation exist` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my corporation exist on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation exist on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation exist on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation exist on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does my corporation exist on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) FALSE
-- Sam, an incorporator: the first directors were not named and have not been elected, so Sam manages; if they were named, Sam does not.
#ASSERT `As an incorporator, do I manage the corporation's affairs now` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`As an incorporator, do I manage the corporation's affairs now` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As an incorporator, do I manage the corporation's affairs now` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `As an incorporator, may I do this act` FALSE FALSE `adopting the original bylaws of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `As an incorporator, may I do this act` TRUE FALSE `electing directors while the incorporators manage the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `As an incorporator, may I do this act` FALSE FALSE `an act that is not necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `What the certificate of incorporation must set forth (section 102(a))`

-- Mei's stock corporation has "Inc." in its name.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No listed word, but a $10,000,000 certificate of total assets and the Division's waiver; one dollar short is not enough.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` `a stock corporation` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000000 FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` `a stock corporation` FALSE FALSE TRUE 9999999 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A nonprofit nonstock association of professionals, in the Division's sole discretion.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` `a stock corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the records` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the records` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the records` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the records` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May my corporation's name contain the word trust` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May my corporation's name contain the word trust` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation's name contain the word trust` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May my corporation's name contain the word bank` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May my corporation's name contain the word bank` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May my corporation's name contain the word bank` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation's name contain the word bank` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation's name contain the word bank` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state the registered office and registered agent as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the certificate state the registered office and registered agent as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the certificate's statement of the corporation's purposes enough` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the certificate's statement of the corporation's purposes enough` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the certificate's statement of the corporation's purposes enough` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this act or activity within my corporation's purposes` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this act or activity within my corporation's purposes` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this act or activity within my corporation's purposes` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- One class of stock with par value stated; two classes lacking the number of each; no classes.
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the certificate state what my nonstock corporation must state` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the certificate state what my nonstock corporation must state` TRUE FALSE)
-- Lena is a member under the stated criteria; where none is stated, she is one if she may vote for the governing body.
#ASSERT `Am I a member of this nonstock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of this nonstock corporation` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a member of this nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May my nonstock corporation make this provision for its members` `a charitable nonstock corporation` `classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my nonstock corporation make this provision for its members` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` `full, limited or no voting rights or powers for a member or class or group of members` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May my nonstock corporation make this provision for its members` `a stock corporation` `classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is an act of my nonstock corporation still valid although it has no members` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an act of my nonstock corporation still valid although it has no members` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my nonstock corporation forfeited or dissolved because it has no members`)
#ASSERT `Does the certificate name the first directors as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the certificate name the first directors as the Law requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the certificate name the first directors as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the certificate name the incorporators` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the certificate name the incorporators` FALSE)

§§ `What the certificate of incorporation may also contain (section 102(b), (c), (d) and (f))`

#ASSERT `Under section 102(b)(1), may the certificate of incorporation contain this provision` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Under section 102(b)(1), may the certificate of incorporation contain this provision` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the certificate of incorporation contain any of the optional matters`)
#ASSERT `May a provision the Law lets the bylaws contain be put in the certificate instead` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May a provision the Law lets the bylaws contain be put in the certificate instead` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has the certificate set out the compromise or arrangement provision in the Law's own words` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the certificate set out the compromise or arrangement provision in the Law's own words` `a charitable nonstock corporation` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the certificate set out the compromise or arrangement provision in the Law's own words` `a stock corporation` FALSE TRUE)
-- Omar, a creditor, may apply; so may a stockholder of a stock corporation but not of a nonstock one (there it is a member); a director is not listed.
#ASSERT `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` `a stock corporation` `a creditor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` `a stock corporation` `a stockholder` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a stockholder` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` `a stock corporation` `a receiver` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` `a stock corporation` `a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Three of five creditors agree, representing 75 of 100 in value, with the court's sanction: binding. At 74, not.
#ASSERT `Is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` 3 5 75 100 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` 3 5 74 100 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` 0 0 0 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Preemptive rights: expressly granted; or in existence on 3 July 1967; not one arising after.
#ASSERT `Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1967 7 3) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1967 7 4) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1967 7 2) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the certificate grant stockholders a preemptive right` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the certificate grant stockholders a preemptive right` FALSE)
-- A larger vote: the Law needs more than 1/2 of the outstanding stock; the certificate asks at least 2/3: larger. Equal: not larger. A bottom of 0 is not a fraction.
#ASSERT `May the certificate require a larger vote than this Law requires` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` 1 2 TRUE 2 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the certificate require a larger vote than this Law requires` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` 1 2 TRUE 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate require a larger vote than this Law requires` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` 1 2 TRUE 1 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate require a larger vote than this Law requires` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` 1 0 TRUE 2 3 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the certificate require a larger number of the directors than this Law requires` 4 5
#ASSERT NOT (`May the certificate require a larger number of the directors than this Law requires` 4 4)
#ASSERT `Does the corporation have perpetual existence` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the corporation have perpetual existence` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2030 12 31))
#ASSERT `Has the duration of the corporation's existence expired on this day` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2030 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the duration of the corporation's existence expired on this day` (YearMonthDay 2030 12 31) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2030 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the duration of the corporation's existence expired on this day` (YearMonthDay 2099 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))
-- Dana, a stockholder, is not liable for the corporation's debts unless a provision (and its conditions) or her own conduct makes her so.
#ASSERT `Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Ravi, a director, sued for a breach of the duty of care after the exculpation provision took effect: protected; for loyalty, bad faith, section 174 or a personal benefit: not.
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Nina, an officer deemed to have consented to service: protected, even for section 174; but not in an action by or in the right of the corporation. An officer who has not so consented: not covered.
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as an officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as an officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as an officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as an officer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A director, in an action by the corporation: that carve-out is the officer's, so a director is still protected.
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An act before the provision took effect is not covered; on the effective date it is.
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A claim that is not for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty is outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` `as a director` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the exculpation provision as it stood at the time of my act still protect me` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exculpation provision as it stood at the time of my act still protect me` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exculpation provision as it stood at the time of my act still protect me` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the certificate set out this power of the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the certificate set out this power of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `the name of the corporation under paragraph (a)(1)` `a stock corporation` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `the classes, number of shares and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue under paragraph (a)(4)` `a stock corporation` TRUE)
#ASSERT `May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `the classes, number of shares and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue under paragraph (a)(4)` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE
#ASSERT `May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `any other provision of the certificate of incorporation` `a stock corporation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `any other provision of the certificate of incorporation` `a stock corporation` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does this count as a fact on which a provision may depend` `the occurrence of an event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this count as a fact on which a provision may depend` `a matter of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paul's company asks whether the certificate may make a stockholder pay the other side's fees: not in an internal corporate claim, nor a claim a stockholder brought.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the certificate make a stockholder liable for fees or expenses in a claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the certificate make a stockholder liable for fees or expenses in a claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the certificate make a stockholder liable for fees or expenses in a claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the certificate make a stockholder liable for fees or expenses in a claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Reserving a name (section 102(e))`

#ASSERT `May I reserve the exclusive right to use this name` `a person intending to incorporate or organize a corporation with that name under this chapter, or contemplating such incorporation or organization` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I reserve the exclusive right to use this name` `another person` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I reserve the exclusive right to use this name` `a foreign corporation intending to qualify to do business in the State of Delaware and adopt that name, or contemplating such qualification and adoption` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my application to reserve the name in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application to reserve the name in the form required` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State reserve the name for me` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State reserve the name for me` TRUE FALSE)
-- Reserved on 1 January 2026, the reservation lasts through 1 May 2026 (120 days); one renewal, through 29 August 2026.
#ASSERT `Through what date does my name reservation last` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) 0 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `Through what date does my name reservation last` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 8 29
#ASSERT `Does my application for renewal renew the reservation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `Does my application for renewal renew the reservation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for renewal renew the reservation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for renewal renew the reservation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT `Has the right to the exclusive use of the reserved name been transferred` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the right to the exclusive use of the reserved name been transferred` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Has the name reservation been cancelled` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the name reservation been cancelled` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State send me back a copy of my filed instrument` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State send me back a copy of my filed instrument` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay with this filing about my name reservation` `the reservation of a name` 75 EQUALS JUST 75
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay with this filing about my name reservation` `another filing` 75 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Signing, acknowledging and filing an instrument (section 103)`

-- Alex signs the certificate with the other incorporators; a later instrument filed before the board is elected goes the same way unless the directors were named.
#ASSERT `Do the incorporators sign this instrument` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Do the incorporators sign this instrument` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the incorporators sign this instrument` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the incorporators sign this instrument` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
